.TP
.BI "attach " "[DIR]"
Attach to an existing repository: read it, show the answers and the gaps, store on approval.
.br
Reads the repository (branches, tags, version and changelog files, test command, CI) and changes nothing in it. Prints the answers it would store, the gaps against the methodology and what it could not determine, and a plan token. With \-\-plan and \-\-approved it stores the answers outside the repository. The gaps are closed, if you want that, by a separate reviewed change. It reads the tree of the methodology's integration branch (develop), else of the default branch, else of HEAD, and says which; never the working tree. It prints origin as read and the https url it normalises to. If answers are already stored it shows stored against detected, lists the fields the stored file lacks, stays read\-only and gives no plan token; with \-\-force the plan replaces what it detects and keeps what it cannot (the roles' models and effort, cloud, memory, budget).
