.BI "rename " "OLD NEW"
Rename a member and its definition.
.RE
.RS
.TP
.BI "refresh " "NAME"
Re\-render a member from the member definition qargi ships now.
.br
Keeps its name, abilities and model. Use it after an upgrade changes the definition (for example its hook); an unchanged member is left alone. Sessions started afterwards use the new definition.
.RE
.RS
.TP
.B models
Show the base members, the profiles with their resolved models and efforts, and each member.
.br
Two base members, one per guard class: worker (build, write, test; may write) and reviewer (review; read\-only). Everything else is a profile {base, tier, effort, purpose} resolved at dispatch: the shipped ones are in lib/model\-defaults.json (build, write, test, review, auditor, advisor, researcher, lead), a project adds or overrides its own under profiles.NAME in its answers, and a provider file (lib/providers/claude.json; the project's models.provider) maps the tiers fast, balanced, deep and frontier to models. The frontier tier (researcher) is opt\-in. Problems are flagged on their row, never fatal: a legacy member (one per ability, retire it after the base exists), a missing base, a refused project profile, a mixed\-class member, a tier with no alias, a frontier member outside researcher. Read\-only.
.RS
