.RE
.TP
.B qargi provider
List and check the model providers: tiers, models and what each can do.
.PP
A provider is a descriptor, lib/providers/NAME.json, with one schema for every provider: the model each tier (fast, balanced, deep, frontier) maps to, with the date and source it was verified, the effort levels it understands, which surfaces it serves (local, cloud) and a capability matrix per surface: model and effort overrides at dispatch, a fixed tool list per agent, a read\-only barrier, a session budget ceiling, memory stores, skills and MCP. A capability that is not verified counts as not supported. A provider with no read\-only barrier on a surface cannot serve the review role there unless you accept that with qargi provider accept. The project's models.provider chooses the provider (default claude).
.RS
