.TP
.BI "check " "[PROJECT]"
Check a Claude Code render for drift (read only).
.br
Needs \-\-target claude\-code. Writes nothing and exits 1 on any finding: library drift (a pack changed or failed review since it was rendered), rendered tampering (a file differs from the manifest, or an extra or missing file), enablement drift (a pack enabled or disabled, or its roles changed, since the render), shadowing of a rendered skill by ~/.claude/skills or by the checkout's .claude/skills, and a missing manifest (nothing rendered yet). It also reports a rendered file that differs from the library copy (even when the manifest was edited with it), a changed file mode, a group\- or world\-writable render, a malformed manifest, and a manifest that names another project or whose role scoping is not advisory.
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-target " "TARGET"
claude\-code renders for a local Claude Code session; managed\-agents (the default for apply) is the cloud update.
.RE
