.SS Lead and credentials
.TP
.B qargi lead
Give, inspect or take away the cloud lead's right to push.
.PP
Only the lead ever pushes, never a member. With a grant it creates agent/* branches and opens pull requests; every merge is asked of you, and it cannot publish releases. grant and revoke are interactive: each step prints its plan and asks you at the terminal, and your answer is the recorded approval. From Claude Code run them with !.
.RS
.TP
.BI "grant " "[PROJECT]"
Guided: create or rotate the grant in three confirmed steps.
.br
Explains how to create the fine\-grained token, checks it, then: token and vault; the GitHub tool; the Push rules. Skips what is in place.
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-from\-file " "FILE"
read the token from a file instead of asking.
.RE
.RE
.RS
.TP
.BI "status " "[PROJECT]"
Show what is in place and what is missing.
.RE
.RS
.TP
.BI "revoke " "[PROJECT]"
Take the grant away.
.br
Removes the tool and the Push rules, detaches and archives the credential, deletes the token file. Revoke the token on GitHub yourself.
.RE
.TP
.B qargi credential
Check or set up the tokens qargi uses.
.PP
Tokens live in files only you can read, outside every repository, and never in a command line, the tracker or the audit log.
.RS
.TP
.BI "check " "[PROJECT]"
Probe the repository token: it must read and should not push.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-write\-token
accept a token that can push, knowingly.
.RE
.RE
.RS
.TP
.BI "setup " "KIND [PROJECT]"
Set up the cloud lead's write token (prefer: qargi lead grant).
.br
Checks the token itself against GitHub (fine\-grained, this repository only, no Administration), stores it mode 600, creates a vault with a bearer credential, attaches it to the lead's deployment and records the grant.
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-from\-file " "FILE"
read the token from a file instead of stdin.
.RE
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-more\-repos
accept a token that can also write to other repositories.
.RE
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-asked " "REQUEST"
the request, in your words, that names the cloud instance; recorded in the audit log.
.RE
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-plan " "TOKEN"
the plan token printed by the same command without \-\-approved.
.RE
.RS
